{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"api_error_status":null,"duration_ms":370429,"duration_api_ms":256938,"ttft_ms":2558,"num_turns":30,"result":"## Summary\n\n**EXP-003: RAG few-shot** — **quality 0.320** (dev), new best (+0.013 vs baseline 0.307)\n\n**What I did:** Created `GoldExemplars.swift` with 12 hard-coded non-dev gold examples. At runtime, for each input, retrieve the 2 nearest exemplars by Jaccard word-overlap similarity and inject them as concrete few-shot demonstrations in the system prompt. Single FM call.\n\n**Result:** \n- 0.320 vs previous best 0.307 — modest but real improvement\n- First tie vs gold (learn_guitar — model asked about guitar type which gold missed)\n- Non-redundancy improved 3→4 across dev cases\n\n**Judge notes insight:** The RAG examples taught the model better redundancy avoidance, but catastrophic coverage failures persist — the model still asks \"What is the name of your bakery?\" for a naming task, and misses critical unknowns (budget for dinner party, departure city for Paris trip). The 3B model sees the good examples but still can't reliably transfer the \"which unknown is most decision-critical\" reasoning to novel task types. Next hypothesis should target this specific failure mode more aggressively (e.g., a chain-of-thought reasoning step asking \"what single fact would most change the plan?\" before generating questions).","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"0d29d5b9-1e74-49f2-be70-e41a5215bbde","total_cost_usd":0.47748925000000003,"usage":{"input_tokens":26,"cache_creation_input_tokens":34611,"cache_read_input_tokens":438120,"output_tokens":14375,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":34611},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":311,"cache_read_input_tokens":33611,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1000,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1000,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":479,"outputTokens":16,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.000559,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000},"claude-sonnet-4-6":{"inputTokens":26,"outputTokens":14375,"cacheReadInputTokens":438120,"cacheCreationInputTokens":34611,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.47693025000000006,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"aa499a10-6382-4721-83e5-61880cc6ddf1"}
{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"api_error_status":null,"duration_ms":482912,"duration_api_ms":219451,"ttft_ms":2050,"num_turns":21,"result":"Iteration complete. Summary:\n\n**Experiment exp004 — `ragCoverageBestOfN`** (best-of-N RAG sets ranked by a deterministic Swift coverage scorer).\n\n- **Hypothesis:** coverage is the wall (budget/who-for/location/timeline/current-state reliably dropped). Sample N full RAG sets at varying temps, then select the best-covering one in Swift — attacking coverage with a deterministic ruler while preserving the natural phrasing of whole model-generated sets.\n- **Result: 0.245 quality (dev) — REGRESSED.** Below best (exp003 = 0.320) and baseline (0.307); spec dropped to 90% (1 error).\n- **Why it failed (honest signal):** A coverage-keyword-only ruler combined with high-temperature sampling backfires. The hotter samples introduced atomicity violations (compound/parenthetical questions) and specificity loss (US tax forms for a German task), and the scorer is blind to those, so it sometimes *selected the worse set*. Coverage itself never moved (still rubric 3).\n- **Takeaway for next time:** selection-by-proxy over the 3B's own samples is insufficient — a useful ruler must score atomicity + specificity + task-fit, not just dimension keyword presence, and sampling needs a low-temp floor. The coverage gap is still the wall; this confirms it's a *capability* limit, not a selection problem.\n\nBuild green ✅, one new run logged ✅ (`results/exp004.json`, `runs.jsonl` run #4), log line prepended to `program.md`. All edits confined to `Sources/DiscoveryAgent/` + `program.md`. Stopping here per the one-experiment rule.","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"b4f6d8a4-f8c2-404b-b53f-1179ef8a7dd6","total_cost_usd":0.8079705,"usage":{"input_tokens":36,"cache_creation_input_tokens":37084,"cache_read_input_tokens":382513,"output_tokens":15368,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":37084},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":647,"cache_read_input_tokens":35725,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1359,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1359,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":479,"outputTokens":16,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.000559,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000},"claude-opus-4-8":{"inputTokens":36,"outputTokens":15368,"cacheReadInputTokens":382513,"cacheCreationInputTokens":37084,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.8074115000000001,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"dbe2f4ea-233c-4dbd-9762-44bca48bb2c0"}
{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"api_error_status":null,"duration_ms":311406,"duration_api_ms":167745,"ttft_ms":3470,"num_turns":17,"result":"Done. One experiment, completed and logged.\n\n**exp005 ragCritiqueRevise** — quality **0.315** (dev), spec 100%, 0 win / 1 tie / 9 loss. **DISCARDED** (−0.005 vs the exp003 best of 0.320).\n\n**What I tried:** A reflexion editor built on the current best. Stage 1 produced the strong RAG few-shot draft (= exp003); stage 2 was a second FM \"auditor\" call given that draft plus an explicit decision-critical dimension checklist (budget / who-for / timeline / scale / location / current-state / goal), instructed to delete already-given/low-value/compound questions, fill the highest-value missing unknown, and keep good questions verbatim to protect naturalness.\n\n**Why it didn't help (the honest signal):** Naturalness held (no robotic regression like the earlier pipelines), but the hard *universal* checklist backfired on coverage — the 3B auditor mechanically injected budget+timeline into tasks where they're noise (bakery naming, GP booking, German tax got \"storage budgets\"), introduced new reworded-overlap redundancy, and even produced a literal \"deadlines or deadlines.\" It swapped one set of wrong slots for another rather than supplying the task-type judgment the model lacks. Coverage stayed at 3.\n\n**Takeaway for next time:** Self-critique can't conjure judgment the base model doesn't have, and a universal checklist is too blunt. The lever should be a **task-conditioned** dimension scaffold (retrieved per task type from the gold bank) rather than reflexion or a global checklist — i.e. keep pushing on richer RAG/distillation.\n\nBuild is green; exactly one new run (`exp005`) logged to `results/runs.jsonl` and `results/exp005.json`.","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"e3f3e3e6-f2c8-4274-b710-054eb666e749","total_cost_usd":0.6270074999999999,"usage":{"input_tokens":28,"cache_creation_input_tokens":36244,"cache_read_input_tokens":335267,"output_tokens":9286,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":36244},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":604,"cache_read_input_tokens":36561,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1067,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1067,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":479,"outputTokens":16,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.000559,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000},"claude-opus-4-8":{"inputTokens":28,"outputTokens":9286,"cacheReadInputTokens":335267,"cacheCreationInputTokens":36244,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.6264485,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"aea31191-ef5a-48cc-94f4-df138d07a758"}
{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"api_error_status":null,"duration_ms":390429,"duration_api_ms":284788,"ttft_ms":3439,"num_turns":31,"result":"Done. One experiment, complete.\n\n**exp006 `ragCoverageScaffold` — quality 0.290 (dev), DISCARDED (−0.030 vs exp003 best 0.320).**\n\n- **Hypothesis:** exp005's insight said the coverage checklist must be *task-conditioned/retrieved*, not universal. So I tagged each gold question with a short decision-critical dimension label, aggregated the dimensions from the same 2 nearest exemplars exp003 retrieves, and injected them as an explicit, adaptable coverage checklist in a single call (avoiding exp005's auditor regressions).\n- **Outcome:** Build green, one new logged run (`results/exp006.json`, run #6). Coverage stayed at 3 and the headline dropped 0.030.\n- **Honest read:** A *retrieved* checklist is no better than a *universal* one. The 3B treats abstract dimension labels as slot-fillers and renders them as vague catch-all or compound questions (wedding \"date AND time\", tax \"deadlines or deadlines\", near-duplicate filed-vs-received pairs). Naming a dimension doesn't supply the judgment to pick the most-critical one or phrase it atomically — it just adds another surface to over-fit. **Both exp005 and exp006 now confirm: explicit dimension menus (universal or task-conditioned) do not fix coverage.** The next lever should inject concrete retrieved gold *questions* as harder constraints (keep/adapt N specific ones) or move to distillation/adapter — not any checklist scaffold.\n\nCurrent best remains **exp003 ragFewShot at 0.320**.","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"960a385f-a193-4211-a467-6443bc203d0b","total_cost_usd":0.9879920000000002,"usage":{"input_tokens":54,"cache_creation_input_tokens":39366,"cache_read_input_tokens":748851,"output_tokens":14668,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":39366},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":546,"cache_read_input_tokens":39514,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1236,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1236,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":479,"outputTokens":16,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.000559,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000},"claude-opus-4-8":{"inputTokens":54,"outputTokens":14668,"cacheReadInputTokens":748851,"cacheCreationInputTokens":39366,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.9874330000000002,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"04b02476-204c-446c-a1cd-9098ca75e549"}
{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"api_error_status":null,"duration_ms":363582,"duration_api_ms":260814,"ttft_ms":4438,"num_turns":20,"result":"Iteration complete. Summary:\n\n**Hypothesis (exp007):** exp003's win came from well-matched few-shot exemplars, but its word-overlap Jaccard retrieval returns ~0 similarity for topically distinct dev queries (resume↔interview, tax↔budget share no words). Replacing it with on-device NLEmbedding sentence-embedding cosine should surface the nearest task TYPE and lift coverage.\n\n**Implementation:** New `SemanticRetrieval.swift` (NLEmbedding cosine + Jaccard fallback), `GoldExemplars.nearestSemantic`, refactored `ragSystemPrompt` to accept overridable exemplars, new `.ragFewShotSemantic` topology, registered as `exp007`. Build green.\n\n**Result: QUALITY 0.273 (dev)** — regressed −0.047 vs the exp003 best of 0.320, and lost exp003's lone tie (now 0/0/10). Coverage stayed flat at 3.\n\n**Honest verdict: DISCARDED — hypothesis falsified.** Better-matched exemplars did not improve coverage; the same failure modes recur verbatim (misses budget/departure-city/who-for, treats tax as document-filing, near-duplicate date questions). The 3B imitates exemplar surface form, not which-unknowns-matter judgment, so topical relevance of exemplars was never the lever. This confirms (again) that retrieval/prompt-context tweaks don't move the coverage wall — pointing to the heavier untried levers (hard keep/adapt-N-gold-questions constraints, or distillation/adapter).\n\nOne new run logged (`results/exp007.json`, `runs.jsonl`), program.md updated, build green. Stopping per the one-experiment rule.","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"a4d45946-5640-4501-a3ce-1ff34b5b6fdf","total_cost_usd":0.8707422499999999,"usage":{"input_tokens":32,"cache_creation_input_tokens":46977,"cache_read_input_tokens":532284,"output_tokens":12411,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_c